            <title>[LU-20976] sanity test_255a: willread/ladvise speed loop hangs, session TIMEOUT</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20976</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Session &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/183cf16c-10e9-4414-99d8-f5395dfdd40b" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sessions/183cf16c-10e9-4414-99d8-f5395dfdd40b&lt;/a&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
(review-dne-ipv6, build 133644) reports sanity test_255a TIMEOUT.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The subtest log (test set &lt;a href="https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/483e26b9-2a1c-47d2-831c-025fd6406f18" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://testing.whamcloud.com/test_sets/483e26b9-2a1c-47d2-831c-025fd6406f18&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;br/&gt;
shows the test working through its 10-iteration willread/OSS-cache/&lt;br/&gt;
ladvise speed comparison loop and stopping partway through iteration 6:&lt;br/&gt;
no further output, no PASS, no FAIL. The session's own timeout fired&lt;br/&gt;
later (230 minutes) while still inside the sanity suite.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The open tickets already linked to test_255a describe a different&lt;br/&gt;
symptom: &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-16449" title="sanity test_255a defect: ladvise failed, test PASS" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-16449"&gt;LU-16449&lt;/a&gt; and &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-15350" title="sanity test_255a defect: ladvise: range [2, 1] is invalid" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-15350"&gt;LU-15350&lt;/a&gt; are about ladvise usage-error text&lt;br/&gt;
printed while the test still PASSes; &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-9069" title="ZFS sanity: FAIL: test_255a Speedup with willread is less than  XX%, got YY%" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-9069"&gt;LU-9069&lt;/a&gt; is about the speed loop&lt;br/&gt;
completing but reporting too small a speedup. None of them is a run&lt;br/&gt;
that produces no result at all. Rainshadow shows this exact signature&lt;br/&gt;
("Timeout occurred after N minutes, last suite running was sanity")&lt;br/&gt;
three times fleet-wide in the last 30 days, none linked to a ticket. A&lt;br/&gt;
JIRA search for "sanity test_255a" status Open finds only the three&lt;br/&gt;
above plus &lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20869" title="reduce run time of long-running tests" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20869"&gt;LU-20869&lt;/a&gt; (general long-test-runtime tracking, not specific&lt;br/&gt;
to this hang).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The patch under test (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-12669" title="FLR-EC: recover data from parity code" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-12669"&gt;LU-12669&lt;/a&gt;) only touches lustre/include/cl_object.h,&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/llite/file.c, lustre/lov/lov_io.c, lustre/obdclass/cl_io.c and&lt;br/&gt;
lustre/tests/sanity-ec.sh, an EC parity-read path unconnected to the&lt;br/&gt;
ladvise willread code test_255a exercises.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Raised by Patch Watcher run pw-engineer-69392-ps2-f06d1f5a7c18 on &lt;a href="https://review.whamcloud.com/69392" class="external-link" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener"&gt;https://review.whamcloud.com/69392&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
